[2026-03-14T22:31:07.338Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KsKVQGnNtYjWnxBgjvBVuj","type":"tool_result","content":"  1681→### ProjectFilters\n  1682→\n  1683→#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Lead, and Team filters\n  1684→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`\n  1685→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the project list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Lead\" dropdown, and \"Team\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n  1686→\n  1687→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all project statuses\n  1688→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`\n  1689→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n  1690→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all project statuses: Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled. Each option has a checkbox for multi-select.\n  1691→\n  1692→#### Test: Status filter filters projects by selected status\n  1693→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Projects exist: \"Auth Rewrite\" (In Progress), \"Mobile App\" (Planned), \"Bug Fixes\" (Completed).\n  1694→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and selects \"In Progress\"\n  1695→- **Expected**: Only \"Auth Rewrite\" is displayed. \"Mobile App\" and \"Bug Fixes\" are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active.\n  1696→\n  1697→#### Test: Status filter allows multi-select\n  1698→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Projects exist with statuses: Planned (1), In Progress (1), Completed (1).\n  1699→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and checks \"Planned\" and \"In Progress\"\n  1700→- **Expected**: Projects with \"Planned\" and \"In Progress\" statuses are shown. \"Completed\" project is hidden. The filter button indicates 2 statuses selected.\n  1701→\n  1702→#### Test: Lead filter dropdown shows all workspace members\n  1703→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\".\n  1704→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Lead\" filter button\n  1705→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all workspace members with their avatars and names. Each option has a checkbox. A searchable input may be present to filter the member list.\n  1706→\n  1707→#### Test: Lead filter filters projects by selected lead\n  1708→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. \"Auth Rewrite\" has lead \"Alice\", \"Mobile App\" has lead \"Bob\", \"API v2\" has no lead.\n  1709→- **Action**: User opens Lead filter and selects \"Alice\"\n  1710→- **Expected**: Only \"Auth Rewrite\" is displayed. \"Mobile App\" and \"API v2\" are hidden. The Lead filter button shows an active indicator.\n  1711→\n  1712→#### Test: Team filter dropdown shows all teams\n  1713→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\".\n  1714→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Team\" filter button\n  1715→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all teams with their names. Each option has a checkbox.\n  1716→\n  1717→#### Test: Team filter filters projects by selected team\n  1718→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. \"Auth Rewrite\" has issues from Engineering only, \"Mobile App\" has issues from Design only, \"API v2\" has issues from both Engineering and Design.\n  1719→- **Action**: User opens Team filter and selects \"Engineering\"\n  1720→- **Expected**: \"Auth Rewrite\" and \"API v2\" are shown (both have Engineering team issues). \"Mobile App\" is hidden.\n  1721→\n  1722→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n  1723→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. \"Auth Rewrite\" (In Progress, lead Alice, Engineering), \"Mobile App\" (In Progress, lead Bob, Design), \"API v2\" (Planned, lead Alice, Engineering).\n  1724→- **Action**: User selects \"In Progress\" in Status filter and \"Alice\" in Lead filter\n  1725→- **Expected**: Only \"Auth Rewrite\" is shown (matches both In Progress status AND lead Alice). \"Mobile App\" and \"API v2\" are hidden.\n  1726→\n  1727→#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all projects\n  1728→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", showing 1 project\n  1729→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n  1730→- **Expected**: All projects are shown again, same as the unfiltered view.\n  1731→\n  1732→#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n  1733→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple projects\n  1734→- **Action**: User applies Status filter for \"Planned\", clears it, applies Lead filter for \"Alice\", clears it, then applies Team filter for \"Design\"\n  1735→- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only projects with Design team issues are shown. Filters remain responsive through multiple interactions.\n  1736→\n  1737→#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n  1738→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n  1739→- **Action**: User selects \"In Progress\" in Status filter\n  1740→- **Expected**: The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge, or different styling). Lead and Team filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n  1741→\n  1742→### CreateProjectModal\n  1743→\n  1744→#### Test: Create Project button opens the create project modal\n  1745→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`, no modal is open\n  1746→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Create Project\" button\n  1747→- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with the title \"Create Project\" or similar. The modal overlays the page with a backdrop. The Name field is focused.\n  1748→\n  1749→#### Test: Create project modal renders all required fields\n  1750→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1751→- **Expected**: The modal displays the following fields: Name (text input, required), Description (text area), Status (dropdown), Lead (searchable member selector), Target date (date picker), Teams (multi-select). \"Create Project\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible at the bottom.\n  1752→\n  1753→#### Test: Create project modal Status dropdown shows all project statuses\n  1754→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1755→- **Action**: User clicks the Status dropdown\n  1756→- **Expected**: Dropdown shows options: Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled. A default status is pre-selected (e.g., \"Planned\").\n  1757→\n  1758→#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector is searchable\n  1759→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. Workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", \"Charlie\".\n  1760→- **Action**: User clicks the Lead selector and types \"Ali\"\n  1761→- **Expected**: The member list filters to show only \"Alice\". User can select \"Alice\" as the lead. The selected lead shows their avatar and name.\n  1762→\n  1763→#### Test: Create project modal Target date uses a date picker\n  1764→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1765→- **Action**: User clicks the Target date field\n  1766→- **Expected**: A date picker opens allowing the user to select a date. After selecting a date (e.g., April 15, 2026), the field displays the selected date.\n  1767→\n  1768→#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector allows multi-select\n  1769→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. Workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\".\n  1770→- **Action**: User clicks the Teams selector, checks \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n  1771→- **Expected**: Both teams are selected and shown as chips/badges in the Teams field. The user can deselect a team by clicking its chip or unchecking it in the dropdown.\n  1772→\n  1773→#### Test: Successful project creation with all fields\n  1774→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1775→- **Action**: User enters \"New Feature\" in Name, \"Build the new feature\" in Description, selects \"In Progress\" status, selects \"Alice\" as lead, picks target date \"2026-05-01\", selects teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\", clicks \"Create Project\"\n  1776→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new project \"New Feature\" appears in the project list with all the specified attributes (status badge \"In Progress\", lead \"Alice\", target date, progress bar at 0%, team icons for Engineering and Design). The project is persisted to the database.\n  1777→\n  1778→#### Test: Successful project creation with only required fields\n  1779→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1780→- **Action**: User enters \"Quick Spike\" in Name, leaves all optional fields empty/default, clicks \"Create Project\"\n  1781→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The project \"Quick Spike\" appears in the project list with the default status, no lead, no target date, and no teams. The project card handles missing optional fields gracefully.\n  1782→\n  1783→#### Test: Create project modal validates name is required\n  1784→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1785→- **Action**: User leaves the Name field empty and clicks \"Create Project\"\n  1786→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown for the Name field (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The modal remains open. No project is created.\n  1787→\n  1788→#### Test: Cancel button closes create project modal without creating\n  1789→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open. User has entered \"Draft Project\" in Name.\n  1790→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1791→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project named \"Draft Project\" is created. The project list remains unchanged.\n  1792→\n  1793→#### Test: Create project modal can be closed by clicking backdrop\n  1794→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1795→- **Action**: User clicks the backdrop/overlay area outside the modal\n  1796→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n  1797→\n  1798→#### Test: Create project modal can be closed with Escape key\n  1799→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1800→- **Action**: User presses the Escape key\n  1801→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No project is created.\n  1802→\n  1803→#### Test: Creating a project and then opening modal again resets fields\n  1804→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has just created a project via the modal\n  1805→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Project\" button again to open the modal\n  1806→- **Expected**: All fields are reset to their defaults (Name is empty, Description is empty, Status is default, Lead is unset, Target date is unset, Teams is unset). No data from the previous creation persists in the form.\n  1807→\n  1808→#### Test: Created project appears immediately in the project list\n  1809→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects` with 2 existing projects\n  1810→- **Action**: User creates a new project \"API v3\" via the create project modal\n  1811→- **Expected**: The project list now shows 3 projects, including the newly created \"API v3\". The new project appears without requiring a page refresh.\n  1812→\n  1813→#### Test: Create project modal Lead selector can be used multiple times\n  1814→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1815→- **Action**: User selects \"Alice\" as lead, then clicks the lead selector again and changes to \"Bob\"\n  1816→- **Expected**: The lead is updated to \"Bob\". The selector works correctly on repeated use. Only one lead can be selected at a time.\n  1817→\n  1818→#### Test: Create project modal Teams selector can be toggled multiple times\n  1819→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create project modal is open\n  1820→- **Action**: User selects \"Engineering\", then also selects \"Design\", then deselects \"Engineering\"\n  1821→- **Expected**: Only \"Design\" remains selected. The multi-select works correctly through multiple toggle interactions.\n  1822→\n  1823→## Project Detail Page (`/project/:projectId`)\n  1824→\n  1825→**Components**: ProjectHeader, ProjectIssuesTab, ProjectOverviewTab\n  1826→\n  1827→### ProjectHeader\n  1828→\n  1829→#### Test: Project header renders all fields for an existing project\n  1830→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/project/1`. Project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists with status \"In Progress\", lead \"Jane Doe\", target date 2026-04-15, and 10 issues (6 completed).\n  1831→- **Expected**: The header displays the project name \"Auth Rewrite\" as an inline-editable text field. A status badge shows \"In Progress\" with appropriate styling. A progress bar shows 60% completion (6/10 issues). The target date \"Apr 15, 2026\" is displayed and inline-editable. The lead shows \"Jane Doe\" with avatar and is inline-editable.\n  1832→\n  1833→#### Test: Inline edit project name\n  1834→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n  1835→- **Action**: User clicks on the project name text, clears it, types \"Auth Rewrite v2\", and presses Enter or clicks away to confirm.\n  1836→- **Expected**: The project name updates to \"Auth Rewrite v2\". The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the name change.\n  1837→\n  1838→#### Test: Inline edit project name — cancel edit\n  1839→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n  1840→- **Action**: User clicks on the project name, types \"Draft Name\", then presses Escape.\n  1841→- **Expected**: The project name reverts to \"Auth Rewrite\". No change is persisted.\n  1842→\n  1843→#### Test: Inline edit project name — validation rejects empty name\n  1844→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project name is \"Auth Rewrite\".\n  1845→- **Action**: User clicks on the project name, clears the field entirely, and presses Enter.\n  1846→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The project name remains \"Auth Rewrite\". No change is persisted.\n  1847→\n  1848→#### Test: Inline edit status badge\n  1849→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\".\n  1850→- **Action**: User clicks the status badge.\n  1851→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing all project statuses: \"Planned\", \"In Progress\", \"Completed\", \"Cancelled\". Each option has distinct styling/color.\n  1852→\n  1853→#### Test: Change project status via inline dropdown\n  1854→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\". Status dropdown is open.\n  1855→- **Action**: User selects \"In Progress\" from the dropdown.\n  1856→- **Expected**: The status badge updates to \"In Progress\" with appropriate color styling. The dropdown closes. The change is persisted to the database. An activity entry is created recording the status change from \"Planned\" to \"In Progress\".\n  1857→\n  1858→#### Test: Change project status multiple times in sequence\n  1859→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project status is \"Planned\".\n  1860→- **Action**: User clicks the status badge, selects \"In Progress\". Then clicks the status badge again and selects \"Completed\".\n  1861→- **Expected**: After first change, status shows \"In Progress\". After second change, status shows \"Completed\". Both changes are persisted. Two separate activity entries are created (one for each change). The progress bar and status badge update correctly each time.\n  1862→\n  1863→#### Test: Inline edit target date via date picker\n  1864→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date is \"Apr 15, 2026\".\n  1865→- **Action**: User clicks the target date field.\n  1866→- **Expected**: A date picker opens showing the current target date pre-selected.\n  1867→\n  1868→#### Test: Change target date\n  1869→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date date picker is open.\n  1870→- **Action**: User selects \"May 1, 2026\" from the date picker.\n  1871→- **Expected**: The target date updates to \"May 1, 2026\". The date picker closes. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the target date change.\n  1872→\n  1873→#### Test: Clear target date\n  1874→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Target date is \"Apr 15, 2026\".\n  1875→- **Action**: User clicks the target date field and clicks a \"Clear\" or remove option.\n  1876→- **Expected**: The target date is removed, displaying a placeholder like \"No target date\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1877→\n  1878→#### Test: Inline edit lead via searchable selector\n  1879→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead is \"Jane Doe\". Workspace members include \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n  1880→- **Action**: User clicks on the lead field.\n  1881→- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown opens listing all workspace members with avatars and names. \"Jane Doe\" is shown as currently selected.\n  1882→\n  1883→#### Test: Change project lead\n  1884→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead selector is open.\n  1885→- **Action**: User types \"Ali\" in the search field, then selects \"Alice Smith\".\n  1886→- **Expected**: The lead updates to \"Alice Smith\" with her avatar. The dropdown closes. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the lead change from \"Jane Doe\" to \"Alice Smith\".\n  1887→\n  1888→#### Test: Search lead selector filters results\n  1889→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead selector is open. Members: \"Jane Doe\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Bob Jones\".\n  1890→- **Action**: User types \"bob\" in the search field.\n  1891→- **Expected**: Only \"Bob Jones\" appears in the filtered results. Other members are hidden.\n  1892→\n  1893→#### Test: Remove project lead\n  1894→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Lead is \"Jane Doe\".\n  1895→- **Action**: User clicks the lead field and selects a \"Remove\" or \"Unassign\" option.\n  1896→- **Expected**: The lead is cleared, showing a placeholder like \"No lead\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1897→\n  1898→#### Test: Progress bar reflects issue completion accurately\n  1899→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`. Project has 10 issues total: 6 Done, 1 Cancelled, 3 In Progress.\n  1900→- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 60% filled (6 completed out of 10 total). A text label or tooltip shows \"6 of 10 issues completed\" or similar.\n  1901→\n  1902→#### Test: Progress bar shows 0% for project with no completed issues\n  1903→- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 5 issues, none completed.\n  1904→- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 0% filled. Text indicates \"0 of 5 issues completed\" or similar.\n  1905→\n  1906→#### Test: Progress bar shows 100% for fully completed project\n  1907→- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 4 issues, all with status \"Done\".\n  1908→- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 100% filled with a fully colored bar.\n  1909→\n  1910→#### Test: Progress bar handles project with no issues\n  1911→- **Initial state**: User is viewing a project with 0 issues.\n  1912→- **Expected**: The progress bar shows 0% or an empty state. No division-by-zero errors occur.\n  1913→\n  1914→#### Test: Header displays tabs for Issues and Overview\n  1915→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1`.\n  1916→- **Expected**: Below the header fields, two tabs are visible: \"Issues\" and \"Overview\". The \"Issues\" tab is active/selected by default.\n  1917→\n  1918→#### Test: Clicking Overview tab switches to overview content\n  1919→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1` with the \"Issues\" tab active.\n  1920→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Overview\" tab.\n  1921→- **Expected**: The \"Overview\" tab becomes active/highlighted. The content area below switches to show the overview content (description, milestones, key metrics). The \"Issues\" tab is no longer highlighted.\n  1922→\n  1923→#### Test: Clicking Issues tab switches back to issues content\n  1924→- **Initial state**: User is viewing `/project/1` with the \"Overview\" tab active.\n  1925→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Issues\" tab.\n  1926→- **Expected**: The \"Issues\" tab becomes active/highlighted. The content area switches to show the project issues list. The \"Overview\" tab is no longer highlighted.\n  1927→\n  1928→#### Test: Navigating to project detail page from project card\n  1929→- **Initial state**: User is on `/projects`. Project \"Auth Rewrite\" exists.\n  1930→- **Action**: User clicks on the \"Auth Rewrite\" project card/name."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPtqE3eZrMWQVAB7Mtxno5","session_id":"d772a1a5-4c71-4d7b-8003-712c0f2c5f45","uuid":"f4876416-43b7-4e33-af95-ad3266a4d54c"}
