[2026-03-14T22:31:27.798Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FPtqE3eZrMWQVAB7Mtxno5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary: Linear-Clone App Exploration\n\nI've conducted a thorough exploration of the linear-clone app. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. Directory Structure\n\n**Key directories in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`:**\n- `/src/components/` - React components including ProjectCard, ProjectFilters, CreateProjectModal\n- `/src/pages/` - Page components including Projects.tsx, ProjectDetail.tsx\n- `/netlify/functions/` - Serverless backend functions\n- `/tests/` - Playwright test files (36 existing .spec.ts files)\n- `/docs/` - Documentation including tests.md (2685 lines)\n- `/scripts/` - Database seed script\n- `/public/` - Static assets\n\n### 2. Test Documentation (docs/tests.md)\n\n**Project Card Tests** (Lines 1623-1668):\n- 11 tests covering project name display as clickable link, status badges with styling, lead display with avatar, target date, progress bar (0%, partial, 100%), team icons, and edge cases (no lead, no date, no issues)\n\n**Projects Page Tests** (Lines 1669-1680):\n- 3 tests: empty state, listing all projects across teams, header and Create Project button\n\n**ProjectFilters Tests** (Lines 1683-1740):\n- 12 tests covering: toolbar rendering with Status/Lead/Team filters, status filter dropdown and multi-select, lead filter with searchable member list, team filter, AND logic between filters, clearing/resetting, active filter indicators\n\n**CreateProjectModal Tests** (Lines 1744-1821):\n- 18 tests covering: modal opening, field rendering, status dropdown, searchable lead selector, date picker, multi-select teams, successful creation (all fields and required only), validation, cancel/escape/backdrop close, field reset, immediate list update\n\n### 3. Existing Test Files\n\nNo project-related spec files exist yet. Current tests are for:\n- Login/Signup (login.spec.ts, signup.spec.ts)\n- Sidebar and navigation\n- My Issues and filters\n- Team Issues and filters\n- Issue detail (header, description, sub-issues, sidebar, activity)\n- Cycles (create, list, detail, burndown)\n- Group by/sort functionality\n\n**Test structure pattern**: Files in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/`\n\n### 4. ProjectCard Component\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ProjectCard.tsx` (114 lines)\n- Displays project name as clickable link to `/project/<projectId>`\n- Status badge with project-specific styling (planned, in_progress, completed, cancelled)\n- Lead section with avatar (initials) and name, or \"No lead\" placeholder\n- Target date with calendar icon or \"No target date\" placeholder\n- Progress bar showing completed/total issues with percentage\n- Team icons showing participating teams (first 2 letters of identifier)\n- Test IDs for all major elements: `project-card-${project.id}`, `project-card-name-${id}`, `project-card-status-${id}`, etc.\n\n**CSS Classes**: ProjectCard.css uses CSS variables and defines:\n- `.project-card` - main container with flex layout\n- `.project-badge-[status]` - status-specific styling\n- `.project-card-progress-fill` - bar fill with green color when 100%\n- `.project-card-team-icon` - small square badges\n\n### 5. Projects Page Component\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Projects.tsx` (117 lines)\n- Header with \"Projects\" title and \"Create Project\" button\n- ProjectFilters component for Status, Lead, Team filtering\n- Filter logic applying AND logic across selected filters\n- Empty state when no projects exist\n- \"No projects match current filters\" when filtered results empty\n- Grid layout rendering ProjectCard components\n- Integration with Redux store for projects, members, teams\n\n### 6. ProjectFilters Component\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/ProjectFilters.tsx` (182 lines)\n- 3 filter controls: Status, Lead, Team\n- Status filter: 4 options (Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled) with multi-select checkboxes\n- Lead filter: searchable dropdown with all members, avatars, and initials\n- Team filter: all teams with checkboxes\n- Active filter indicators (badge showing count of selected items)\n- Click-outside detection to close dropdowns\n- Test IDs: `project-filter-btn-[type]`, `project-filter-dropdown-[type]`, `project-filter-option-[type]-[value]`\n\n### 7. CreateProjectModal Component\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateProjectModal.tsx` (363 lines)\n- Fields: Name (required), Description (textarea), Status (dropdown), Lead (searchable), Target date (date input), Teams (multi-select)\n- Status options: Planned (default), In Progress, Completed, Cancelled\n- Lead selector with search input and filterable member list\n- Date input (native HTML5 date picker)\n- Teams multi-select with chip display of selected teams\n- Form reset when modal opens\n- Escape key and backdrop click to close\n- Form validation (name required)\n- Test IDs: `create-project-modal`, `create-project-name-input`, `create-project-status-selector`, etc.\n\n### 8. Netlify Functions (Backend)\n\n**Projects GET/POST** (`/netlify/functions/projects.ts`):\n- GET: Fetches all projects with lead info, issue counts (total and completed), team info\n- POST: Creates new project with name (required), description, status (default \"planned\"), leadId, targetDate\n- Returns enriched project data with team maps and member/team lists for filters\n\n**Project Detail GET** (`/netlify/functions/project-detail.ts`):\n- Fetches single project with full details, issues grouped by team, milestones, members, labels, activity\n\n**Update Project PUT** (`/netlify/functions/update-project.ts`):\n- Updates project fields with activity logging\n\n### 9. Seed Data\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- Creates workspace \"Acme Corp\" with 3 members: Alice Johnson, Bob Smith, Carol Davis\n- Creates 2 teams: Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- Creates 1 project: \"V2 Launch\" (in_progress status, lead: Alice, target date: 2026-06-30)\n- Creates issues across both teams linked to the project\n- Creates labels, cycles, milestones, notifications\n\n### 10. Playwright Config\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Timeout: 60 seconds\n- Uses Replay.io for recording\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Fully parallel execution enabled\n- No retries\n\n### Key Test IDs Pattern Used Throughout\n\nThe codebase follows consistent naming: `[component]-[field|type]-[action|id]`\n- Examples: `project-card-${id}`, `project-filter-btn-status`, `create-project-modal`, `project-card-progress-${id}`\n\nAll components are ready for Playwright test implementation with well-structured test IDs and clear component interfaces."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a83aefaba1b0e9995 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 66892\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 40792</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d772a1a5-4c71-4d7b-8003-712c0f2c5f45","uuid":"00729b5e-f5ec-4a15-a622-1ca6f0085d5e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the linear-clone app in /repo/apps/. I need to understand:\n1. The directory structure (list key directories and files)\n2. Find docs/tests.md - specifically the test entries related to \"Project card\" and \"Projects page\" (including filters)\n3. Find any existing test files (*.spec.ts)\n4. Find the ProjectCard component and Projects page component\n5. Find the playwright config\n6. Find the seed data file\n7. Find Netlify functions related to projects\n\nBe thorough - read the test entries, component files, and any existing spec files.","agentId":"a83aefaba1b0e9995","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summa